    "title": "Northern Gannet",
    "summary": "<p><img alt=\"Northern Gannet\" src=\"https://static.inaturalist.org/photos/716984157/large.jpg\" /></p><p>Northern Gannet, in Pillar Point Harbor, CA, US</p><p>This is Morris.</p> <p>Morris is a local celebrity: the only known Northern Gannet (<em>Morus bassanus</em>) in the entire Pacific Ocean.</p> <p>He showed up in the Farallon Islands off the coast of San Francisco <a href=\"https://baynature.org/magazine/spring2017/atlantic-bird-makes-home-california-maybe-melting-arctic-ice/\">14 years ago</a>. He has since made Pillar Point harbor his home, where he's quite easy to spot: the only white bird with a yellow head, usually hanging out with the smaller black Brandt’s cormorants near the harbor sign visible from the end of the commercial pier.</p> <p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net...",
